{
  "metadata": {
    "title": "API Fetch & Table Visualizer",
    "target_domain": "*",
    "language": "javascript",
    "created_at": 1773446400000,
    "updated_at": 1773446400000
  },
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_intro",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# 📊 REST API Fetcher & Interactive Data Visualizer\nThis notebook demonstrates how to query public REST APIs from Chrome Lite, transform nested JSON responses, and render interactive sortable data tables right inside your notebook cells."
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_fetch_users_header",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 1. Fetching Remote API Data (JSONPlaceholder Users)\nExecutes an asynchronous HTTP GET request and normalizes the payload into a clean tabular structure:"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_fetch_users_code",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "const response = await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users');\nconst users = await response.json();\n\n// Flatten nested objects (address, company) into table columns\nreturn users.map(u => ({\n  ID: u.id,\n  Name: u.name,\n  Username: u.username,\n  Email: u.email,\n  City: u.address?.city || 'N/A',\n  Company: u.company?.name || 'N/A',\n  Website: u.website\n}));"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_crypto_header",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 2. Real-Time Market Data (CoinGecko Public API)\nFetches live cryptocurrency prices and market stats:"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_crypto_code",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "const res = await fetch('https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/coins/markets?vs_currency=usd&order=market_cap_desc&per_page=10&page=1&sparkline=false');\nconst coins = await res.json();\n\nreturn coins.map(c => ({\n  Rank: c.market_cap_rank,\n  Symbol: c.symbol.toUpperCase(),\n  Name: c.name,\n  Price_USD: `$${c.current_price.toLocaleString()}`,\n  Change_24h: `${c.price_change_percentage_24h?.toFixed(2)}%`,\n  Market_Cap: `$${(c.market_cap / 1e9).toFixed(2)}B`\n}));"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_github_header",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 3. Querying GitHub Public Repositories\nFetches trending web technology repositories from the GitHub Search API:"
    },
    {
      "id": "cell_github_code",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "const res = await fetch('https://api.github.com/search/repositories?q=electron+stars:>5000&sort=stars&order=desc');\nconst data = await res.json();\n\nreturn (data.items || []).slice(0, 10).map(repo => ({\n  Repository: repo.full_name,\n  Stars: repo.stargazers_count.toLocaleString(),\n  Forks: repo.forks_count.toLocaleString(),\n  Language: repo.language || 'Multi',\n  URL: repo.html_url\n}));"
    }
  ]
}
